IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgd-compromise`
IMPORT `sgd-amalgamation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 7, ss 215I and 215J (the solvency statements of an amalgamation).
-- Section 215I defines the solvency statement "in relation to an amalgamating company" for section 215C(2)(b); section 215J defines it
-- "in relation to an amalgamated company" for sections 215C(2)(c) and 215D(5). Both define their own: the keel's s 7A is for other proposals and is not used here.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes a person's point of view; the seat layer (sgd-seat.l4) does.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the Guide's rulings; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgd)").
--   JUST TRUE   the section's own test is met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to this case in its own words (a "means" definition, a condition introduced by "if", "unless",
--               "until"; a list closed with "only"; a flat negative; a period or "where" condition the text states).
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, points to a power or
--               instrument outside the sources, or limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Whether a company is exempt from audit under section 205B or 205C is another part's rule: an input here (as in the keel's s 7A(2)).
-- The penalty record is `s 210(9) penalty`, declared once in sgd-compromise.l4 (months of imprisonment, as the text counts them here: 3 years is 36 months).

§ `Section 215I: the solvency statement in relation to an amalgamating company`

-- Headings (lines 21513-21514): "Solvency statement in relation to amalgamating company and offence for making false statement": not operative.

-- What the statement says and how it was made out, as a witness could read it off the document.
DECLARE `s 215I statement` HAS
    `s 215I(1) it is a statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215I(1)(a) it says the board has formed the opinion that, as regards the amalgamating company's situation at the date of the statement, there is no ground on which the amalgamating company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215I(1)(b) it says the board has formed the opinion that, at the date of the statement, the value of the amalgamating company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215I(2) it is in the form of a written declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215I(2)(b) it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the amalgamating company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): "For the purposes of section 215C(2)(b), “solvency statement”, in relation to an amalgamating company, means a statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company that it has formed the opinion (a) that, as regards the
-- amalgamating company’s situation at the date of the statement, there is no ground on which the amalgamating company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts; and (b) that, at the date of the statement, the value of the amalgamating
-- company’s assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities), being a statement which complies with subsection (2)." This function is the content, (a) and (b).
-- src:21516 | 215I.—(1) For the purposes of section 215C(2)(b), “solvency
-- src:21517 | statement”, in relation to an amalgamating company, means a
-- src:21518 | statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company
-- src:21519 | that it has formed the opinion —
-- src:21521 | (a) that, as regards the amalgamating company’s situation at
-- src:21522 | the date of the statement, there is no ground on which the
-- src:21527 | amalgamating company could then be found to be unable
-- src:21528 | to pay its debts; and
-- src:21530 | (b) that, at the date of the statement, the value of the
-- src:21531 | amalgamating company’s assets is not less than the value
-- src:21532 | of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities),
-- src:21534 | being a statement which complies with subsection (2).
@ref s 215I(1) (src:21516-21534)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 215I statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(1) the statement has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    (statement's `s 215I(1) it is a statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company`)
      AND (statement's `s 215I(1)(a) it says the board has formed the opinion that, as regards the amalgamating company's situation at the date of the statement, there is no ground on which the amalgamating company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts`)
      AND (statement's `s 215I(1)(b) it says the board has formed the opinion that, at the date of the statement, the value of the amalgamating company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“solvency statement”, in relation to an amalgamating company, means a statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company that it has formed the opinion — (a) that, as regards the amalgamating company’s situation at the date of the statement" (a "means" definition)

-- (2): "The solvency statement (a) if the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, must be in the form of a written declaration; or (b) if the amalgamating company is not such a company, must be in the form of
-- a written declaration or must be accompanied by a report from its auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the amalgamating company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances."
-- src:21536 | (2) The solvency statement —
-- src:21538 | (a) if the amalgamating company is exempt from audit
-- src:21539 | requirements under section 205B or 205C, must be in
-- src:21540 | the form of a written declaration; or
-- src:21542 | (b) if the amalgamating company is not such a company, must
-- src:21543 | be in the form of a written declaration or must be
-- src:21544 | accompanied by a report from its auditor that the auditor
-- src:21545 | has inquired into the affairs of the amalgamating company
-- src:21546 | and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable
-- src:21547 | given all the circumstances.
@ref s 215I(2) (src:21536-21547)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 215I statement`
      `the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
    THEN (IF statement's `s 215I(2) it is in the form of a written declaration`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C, must be in the form of a written declaration" (a duty not met; the provision's own question; a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
    ELSE (IF    (statement's `s 215I(2) it is in the form of a written declaration`)
             OR (statement's `s 215I(2)(b) it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the amalgamating company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the amalgamating company is not such a company, must be in the form of a written declaration or must be accompanied by a report from its auditor" (a duty not met; the provision's own question; a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- (1) as a whole: the content and the form: "being a statement which complies with subsection (2)". A "means" definition for the purposes of section 215C(2)(b).
-- src:21516 | 215I.—(1) For the purposes of section 215C(2)(b), “solvency
-- src:21517 | statement”, in relation to an amalgamating company, means a
-- src:21518 | statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company
-- src:21519 | that it has formed the opinion —
