-- src:21532 | of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities),
-- src:21534 | being a statement which complies with subsection (2).
@ref s 215I(1) whole (src:21516-21534)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 215I statement`
      `the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(1) the statement is a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company for the purposes of section 215C(2)(b)` MEANS
    IF    (`s 215I(1) the statement has the content the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND (`s 215I(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` statement `the amalgamating company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a statement by the board of directors of the amalgamating company that it has formed the opinion ... being a statement which complies with subsection (2)" (a "means" definition)

-- (3): "In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)."
-- src:21551 | (3) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:21552 | (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the
-- src:21553 | amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 215I(3) (src:21551-21553)
GIVEN `the directors took into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(3) the directors have formed the opinion as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the directors took into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (4): "In determining, for the purposes of subsection (1)(b), whether the value of the amalgamating company’s assets is or will become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities), the board of directors of the amalgamating company
-- (a) must have regard to (i) the most recent financial statements of the amalgamating company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be; and (ii) all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value ...; and
-- (b) may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities that are reasonable in the circumstances."
