@ref s 215I(4)(a) (src:21555-21576)
GIVEN `the board had regard to the most recent financial statements of the amalgamating company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board had regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the amalgamating company's assets and the value of the amalgamating company's liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(4)(a) the board has had regard to what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the board had regard to the most recent financial statements of the amalgamating company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be`
      AND `the board had regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the amalgamating company's assets and the value of the amalgamating company's liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the board of directors of the amalgamating company — (a) must have regard to — (i) the most recent financial statements of the amalgamating company that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be; and (ii) all other circumstances" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

