GIVEN `the valuation or estimate is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(4)(b) the board may rely on the valuation or estimate` MEANS
    IF `the valuation or estimate is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities that are reasonable in the circumstances" (a grant whose limit is not met; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215I-1)

-- (5): "In determining, for the purposes of subsection (4), the value of a contingent liability, the board of directors of the amalgamating company may take into account (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and (b) any claim the amalgamating company is entitled
-- to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability."
-- src:21580 | (5) In determining, for the purposes of subsection (4), the value of a
-- src:21581 | contingent liability, the board of directors of the amalgamating
-- src:21582 | company may take into account —
-- src:21584 | (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and
-- src:21586 | (b) any claim the amalgamating company is entitled to make
-- src:21587 | and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or
-- src:21588 | extinguish the contingent liability.
@ref s 215I(5) (src:21580-21588)
GIVEN `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a claim the amalgamating company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(5) the board may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` MEANS
    IF    `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring`
       OR `the matter is a claim the amalgamating company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed; fork F-215I-3): "may take into account — (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and (b) any claim" lists two matters without "only", and says nothing of any other

-- (6): "Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both."
-- src:21590 | (6) Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour
-- src:21591 | of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be
-- src:21592 | made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed
-- src:21593 | in it shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:21594 | fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:21595 | exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 215I(6) (src:21590-21595)
GIVEN `the person is a director of an amalgamating company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215I(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of an amalgamating company`
      AND `the person votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made`
      AND (NOT `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-215I-2): "Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 215I(6) penalty (src:21590-21595)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
`s 215I(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
    THEN JUST (`s 210(9) penalty` OF 100000, 36, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both": 3 years is 36 months, and the text allows both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 215J: the solvency statement in relation to an amalgamated company`

-- Headings (lines 21597-21598): "Solvency statement in relation to amalgamated company and offence for making false statement": not operative.

DECLARE `s 215J statement` HAS
    `s 215J(1) it is a written declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215J(1) it is by the board of directors of each amalgamating company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215J(1)(a) it says the board has formed the opinion that the amalgamated company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due as at the date on which the amalgamation is to become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215J(1)(b) it says the board has formed the opinion that the value of the amalgamated company's assets will not be less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): "In sections 215C(2)(c) and 215D(5), “solvency statement”, in relation to an amalgamated company, means a written declaration by the board of directors of each amalgamating company that it has formed the opinion (a) that the amalgamated company will be able
-- to pay its debts as they fall due as at the date on which the amalgamation is to become effective; and (b) that the value of the amalgamated company’s assets will not be less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)." A "means" definition.
-- src:21600 | 215J.—(1) In sections 215C(2)(c) and 215D(5), “solvency
-- src:21601 | statement”, in relation to an amalgamated company, means a
-- src:21602 | written declaration by the board of directors of each amalgamating
-- src:21603 | company that it has formed the opinion —
-- src:21605 | (a) that the amalgamated company will be able to pay its debts
-- src:21606 | as they fall due as at the date on which the amalgamation is
-- src:21607 | to become effective; and
-- src:21609 | (b) that the value of the amalgamated company’s assets will
-- src:21610 | not be less than the value of its liabilities (including
-- src:21611 | contingent liabilities).
@ref s 215J(1) (src:21600-21611)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 215J statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215J(1) the statement is a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company for the purposes of sections 215C(2)(c) and 215D(5)` MEANS
    IF    (statement's `s 215J(1) it is a written declaration`)
      AND (statement's `s 215J(1) it is by the board of directors of each amalgamating company`)
      AND (statement's `s 215J(1)(a) it says the board has formed the opinion that the amalgamated company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due as at the date on which the amalgamation is to become effective`)
      AND (statement's `s 215J(1)(b) it says the board has formed the opinion that the value of the amalgamated company's assets will not be less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“solvency statement”, in relation to an amalgamated company, means a written declaration by the board of directors of each amalgamating company that it has formed the opinion" (a "means" definition)

-- (2): "In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)."
-- src:21615 | (2) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:21616 | (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the
-- src:21617 | amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 215J(2) (src:21615-21617)
GIVEN `the directors took into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215J(2) the directors have formed the opinion as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the directors took into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (3): "In determining, for the purposes of subsection (1)(b), whether the value of the amalgamated company’s assets will become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities), the board of directors of each amalgamating company
-- (a) must have regard to (i) the most recent financial statements of the amalgamating company and the other amalgamating companies that comply with section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be; and (ii) all other circumstances ...; and
-- (b) may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities that are reasonable in the circumstances."
