-- src:21653 | and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or
-- src:21654 | extinguish the contingent liability.
@ref s 215J(4) (src:21646-21654)
GIVEN `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a claim the amalgamated company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215J(4) the board may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` MEANS
    IF    `the matter is the likelihood of the contingency occurring`
       OR `the matter is a claim the amalgamated company is entitled to make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish the contingent liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed; fork F-215I-3): "may take into account — (a) the likelihood of the contingency occurring; and (b) any claim" lists two matters without "only", and says nothing of any other

-- (5): "Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both."
-- src:21656 | (5) Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour
-- src:21657 | of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be
-- src:21658 | made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed
-- src:21659 | in it shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:21660 | fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:21661 | exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 215J(5) (src:21656-21661)
GIVEN `the person is a director of an amalgamating company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215J(5) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of an amalgamating company`
      AND `the person votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made`
      AND (NOT `the director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-215I-2): "Any director of an amalgamating company who votes in favour of or otherwise causes a solvency statement under this section to be made without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 215J(5) penalty (src:21656-21661)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
`s 215J(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
    THEN JUST (`s 210(9) penalty` OF 100000, 36, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both": 3 years is 36 months, and the text allows both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of ss 215I and 215J that name a party and an act`

-- The directors' duties in forming the opinion. No time limit and no consequence of their own in the text (the offence of subsection (6) or (5) is the consequence of making a statement without reasonable grounds): no breach path.
DECLARE `s 215I act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215I(3) take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)`
    `s 215I(4)(a) have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances`
    `s 215J(2) take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)`
    `s 215J(3)(a) have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances`

-- src:21551 | (3) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:21552 | (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the
-- src:21553 | amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 215I(3) rule (src:21551-21553)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215I act`
`s 215I(3) a director must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 215I(3) take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215I(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not take into account all liabilities of the amalgamating company (including contingent liabilities)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:21555 | (4) In determining, for the purposes of subsection (1)(b), whether
-- src:21556 | the value of the amalgamating company’s assets is or will become
-- src:21557 | less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities),
-- src:21558 | the board of directors of the amalgamating company —
-- src:21560 | (a) must have regard to —
-- src:21562 | (i) the most recent financial statements of the
-- src:21563 | amalgamating company that comply with
-- src:21564 | section 201(2) and (5), as the case may be; and
-- src:21566 | (ii) all other circumstances that the directors know or
-- src:21567 | ought to know affect, or may affect, the value of the
-- src:21568 | amalgamating company’s assets and the value of the
-- src:21569 | amalgamating company’s liabilities (including
-- src:21570 | contingent liabilities); and
-- src:21575 | (b) may rely on valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities
-- src:21576 | that are reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 215I(4)(a) rule (src:21555-21576)
GIVEN `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 215C party` `s 215I act`
`s 215I(4)(a) the board must have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances` MEANS
    PARTY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company`
    MUST `s 215I(4)(a) have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215I(4)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:21615 | (2) In forming an opinion for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and
-- src:21616 | (b), the directors must take into account all liabilities of the
-- src:21617 | amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities).
@ref s 215J(2) rule (src:21615-21617)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215I act`
`s 215J(2) a director must take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 215J(2) take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215J(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not take into account all liabilities of the amalgamated company (including contingent liabilities)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

