    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 215J(3)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not have regard to the most recent financial statements and all other circumstances" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
